Subject: [PATCH] minimum arm64: ship WebPositive

WebPositive is not compiled here: `src/apps/webpositive/Jamfile` only
builds it when `haikuwebkit_devel` is available, and turning that build
feature on means linking this tree against a full browser engine, which is
a different undertaking from packaging one. Instead this adds the already
prebuilt `webpositive` package straight to the image, the same way 0012
adds prebuilt curl/wget/tar/gzip rather than building them from source.

webpositive needs haikuwebkit (the engine) at runtime, sqlite3 (its cookie
jar and web storage), dav1d and libavif1.0 (AV1/AVIF image decoding), and
noto_sans_cjk_kr (without it Korean/Japanese/Chinese draw as empty boxes).
None of the five are on HaikuPorts for arm64, so -- like curl/wget/tar/gzip
-- they are declared in the arm64 repository list and expected to be
staged into the generated directory's download/ before the build; the
hpkg files are in ../packages/, and add-media-arm64.sh copies them there.

haikuwebkit_devel is deliberately not listed: nothing in this image links
against it, only the base haikuwebkit runtime it depends on.

Also declares openssl3 and openssl3_devel, which turned out not to be
declared anywhere despite 0008 already listing openssl3 in
AddHaikuImageSystemPackages for the root-certificate fix. That worked only
by accident, carried by a hpkg that had been placed in some earlier build's
download/ by hand and never captured in a patch: AddRepositoryPackage
silently drops any package with no matching file under HAIKU_NO_DOWNLOADS=1
rather than failing the build, so the gap went unnoticed until haikuwebkit
needed lib:libcrypto and the dependency solver had nothing to offer it.
curl and wget need it too (lib:libssl); their own patch (0012) happened to
predate anyone building with HAIKU_NO_DOWNLOADS=1 and a clean download/, so
the gap is fixed here instead, where it first became impossible to miss.

diff --git a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
index 7bf5f19b82..2999e2ae6b 100644
--- a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
+++ b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
@@ -209,6 +209,23 @@ rule DefineDefaultBuildProfiles
 					wget
 					;
 			}
+
+			# WebPositive itself, and the packages it needs that HaikuPorts does
+			# not publish for arm64: HaikuWebKit, sqlite3 (its cookie jar and
+			# web storage), dav1d and libavif1.0 (AV1/AVIF image decoding), and
+			# CJK glyphs, without which Korean/Japanese/Chinese draw as boxes.
+			# All are prebuilt for arm64 and published in RENKU Apps -- webkit
+			# is a full browser engine, not something this build compiles.
+			if $(TARGET_PACKAGING_ARCH) = arm64 {
+				AddHaikuImageSystemPackages
+					dav1d
+					haikuwebkit
+					libavif1.0
+					noto_sans_cjk_kr
+					sqlite3
+					webpositive
+					;
+			}
 		}

 		case "test-*" : {
diff --git a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64 b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
index a702c4a83c..fecbe51d03 100644
--- a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
+++ b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
@@ -6,9 +6,18 @@ RemotePackageRepository HaikuPorts
 	ca_root_certificates-2025_12_02-1
 	haikuporter-0_bootstrap-1
 	noto-20170202_bootstrap-7
+	noto_sans_cjk_kr-2.004-1
 	:
 	# repository architecture packages
 	# primary architecture (arm64)
+	# Not on HaikuPorts for arm64 either (see the curl/wget note below): TLS
+	# for curl, wget and HaikuWebKit alike. Also what lets openssl3's own
+	# AddHaikuImageSystemPackages entry in DefaultBuildProfiles resolve --
+	# without a hpkg here HAIKU_NO_DOWNLOADS=1 drops it from the local
+	# repository index silently, and every https request, pkgman's included,
+	# fails much later with "certificate verify failed".
+	openssl3-3.5.4-1
+	openssl3_devel-3.5.4-1
 	bash-5.3_bootstrap-1
 	binutils-2.41_2026_03_10_bootstrap-1
 	bison-3.8.2_bootstrap-1
@@ -53,6 +62,15 @@ RemotePackageRepository HaikuPorts
 	gzip-1.13-1
 	tar-1.35-1
 	wget-1.24.5-1
+	# WebPositive and its remaining runtime dependencies -- also not on
+	# HaikuPorts for arm64. webpositive is prebuilt (this tree is not asked
+	# to compile a browser engine); haikuwebkit_devel is deliberately not
+	# listed, since nothing here links against it.
+	dav1d-1.4.3-1
+	haikuwebkit-1.10.0-3
+	libavif1.0-1.1.1-1
+	sqlite3-3.50.4-1
+	webpositive-r1~beta6_hrev99000_dirty-1
 	:
 	# source packages
 	bash
